SELECT 5733 AS id, count(*) AS matching_rows FROM news_items WHERE id = 5733 AND headline = $ch$Giza (Pyramids) served as secondary necropolis before Khufu's pyramid$ch$ AND summary = $cs$Giza (Pyramids) served as secondary necropolis before Khufu's pyramid. Conservatively dated to late 3rd dynasty or early 4th dynasty during Khufu's reign Could be even older with little excavation and analysis undertaken Risner believed Giza (Pyramids) was occupied and used as a necropolis before Khufu$cs$ AND post_text = $cp$Researchers conservatively date the Wadi Cemetery to the late 3rd or early 4th dynasty, though it could be older with little analysis undertaken. Some scholars believed Giza was occupied as a necropolis before Khufu. Before rising to prominence, Giza held secondary status to Saqqara, Maidum, and Dashur. The Western Cemetery and Wadi Cemetery add to growing evidence of pre-Khufu archaeology at Giza. Research by Mark Lehner and Zahi Hawass also suggests a pre-Khufu settlement existed there.$cp$ AND facts = $cf$["Conservatively dated to late 3rd dynasty or early 4th dynasty during Khufu's reign", "Could be even older with little excavation and analysis undertaken", "Risner believed Giza (Pyramids) was occupied and used as a necropolis before Khufu", "Secondary status to Saqqara, Maidum and Dashur before rising to prominence with Khufu's pyramid project", "Western cemetery and Wadi cemetery added to growing list of pre-Khufu archaeology at Giza (Pyramids)", "Researchers科尔 Chromemer and Regillo evidence suggests pre-Khufu town at Giza (Pyramids)"]$cf$::jsonb
UNION ALL
SELECT 5797 AS id, count(*) AS matching_rows FROM news_items WHERE id = 5797 AND headline = $ch$Academia uses biased dating methods influenced by Bible$ch$ AND summary = $cs$Academia uses biased dating methods influenced by Bible. The 'DiCaprio dating' system confuses minimum with maximum dates Archaeologists date to the youngest spectrum possible 19th century scholars pushed a 6,000-year date based on Bible calculations$cs$ AND post_text = $cp$Some researchers argue archaeological dating methods have存在的问题 — Göbekli Tepe was dated to the Pre-Pottery Neolithic (c. 9500–8000 BCE) using radiocarbon dating, which confirmed earlier suspicions of its great age. The debate over dating methodologies continues within the field.$cp$ AND facts = $cf$["The 'DiCaprio dating' system confuses minimum with maximum dates", "Archaeologists date to the youngest spectrum possible", "19th century scholars pushed a 6,000-year date based on Bible calculations", "Göbekli Tepe was only accepted as 9,000 years old after carbon dating became available", "If discovered 20 years earlier, it would not have been attributed to its current age", "Carbon dating is rarely done on old structures due to funding priorities"]$cf$::jsonb
UNION ALL
SELECT 6266 AS id, count(*) AS matching_rows FROM news_items WHERE id = 6266 AND headline = $ch$伪造说逻辑漏洞：1960年代无精密加工能力$ch$ AND summary = $cs$伪造说逻辑漏洞：1960年代无精密加工能力. 若为伪造需使用现代五轴CNC机床研磨花岗岩，成本极高 1960-1980年代容器价值不高，不值得如此高成本伪造 普通古董商不会使用中国机床大量生产无装饰的石容器$cs$ AND post_text = $cp$若为伪造需使用现代五轴CNC机床研磨花岗岩，成本极高。1960-1980年代容器价值不高，不值得如此高成本伪造。普通古董商不会使用中国机床大量生产无装饰的石容器。容器具有复杂的数学设计和径向遍历图案，带把握把的容器具有复杂几何形状，无法仅用车床制造。至少部分容器可追溯到1980年代倒卖至1960年代，当时尚无计算机控制机床。$cp$ AND facts = $cf$["若为伪造需使用现代五轴CNC机床研磨花岗岩，成本极高", "1960-1980年代容器价值不高，不值得如此高成本伪造", "普通古董商不会使用中国机床大量生产无装饰的石容器", "容器具有复杂的数学设计和径向遍历图案", "带握把的容器具有复杂几何形状，无法仅用车床制造", "至少部分容器可追溯到1980年代或1960年代，当时尚无计算机控制机床"]$cf$::jsonb
UNION ALL
SELECT 6342 AS id, count(*) AS matching_rows FROM news_items WHERE id = 6342 AND headline = $ch$Geologists debate natural volcanic formation vs人工 structure$ch$ AND summary = $cs$Geologists debate natural volcanic formation vs人工 structure. Discussion centers on whether the formation is natural or constructed One hypothesis is that it could be a volcanic dyke Comparison made to megalithic structures observed in Peru$cs$ AND post_text = $cp$The Natural Wall remains a mystery. One side looks like a volcanic dyke, but the block-like appearance on the other side resembles megalithic structures found in Peru. Some blocks even have rolled edges like placed stones. Locals weigh in on the debate 🗿

Note: The formation is officially called the 'Natural Wall' and is described by geologists as a resistant vertical bed of Jacobsville Sandstone, not a volcanic dyke. The volcanic dyke hypothesis is one proposed by non-expert observers to explain its appearance.$cp$ AND facts = $cf$["Discussion centers on whether the formation is natural or constructed", "One hypothesis is that it could be a volcanic dyke", "Comparison made to megalithic structures observed in Peru", "On one side, the formation appears more block-like and constructed", "On the other side, the rock appears more naturally fractured like a volcanic dyke should", "Local Michigan experts give their opinion on the formation", "The formation has rolled edges on some blocks, similar to placed stones", "Water runs through the ravine with multiple veins crossing the area"]$cf$::jsonb
UNION ALL
SELECT 8351 AS id, count(*) AS matching_rows FROM news_items WHERE id = 8351 AND headline = $ch$Локалитет Беловоде код Петровца на Млави furnaces: earliest secure copper smelting evidence worldwide, dated to 4900 BC$ch$ AND summary = $cs$Локалитет Беловоде код Петровца на Млави furnaces: earliest secure copper smelting evidence worldwide, dated to 4900 BC. Excavations at Локалитет Беловоде код Петровца на Млави and Pločnik led by archaeometallurgist Miljana Radivojević uncovered copper slag, malachite beads, and metal droplets in Vinča-period contexts Results confirmed through chemical and microstructural analysis, published in a 2021 monograph Pushed back confirmed date of true copper smelting to 4900 BC, making Локалитет Беловоде код Петровца на Млави the earliest secure evidence of extractive metallurgy anywhere in the world$cs$ AND post_text = $cp$Archaeometallurgist Miljana Radivojević's excavations at Локалитет Беловоде код Петровца на Млави and Pločnik uncovered copper slag, malachite beads, and metal droplets in Vinča-period layers, confirmed by chemical and microstructural analysis published in a 2010 Journal of Archaeological Science paper. This pushes confirmed copper smelting to c. 5000 BC, making Локалитет Беловоде код Петровца на Млави the earliest secure evidence of extractive metallurgy in Europe. Rudna Glava is one of the earliest known copper mines, mined at scale. Incredible! 🔥⚒️$cp$ AND facts = $cf$["Excavations at Локалитет Беловоде код Петровца на Млави and Pločnik led by archaeometallurgist Miljana Radivojević uncovered copper slag, malachite beads, and metal droplets in Vinča-period contexts", "Results confirmed through chemical and microstructural analysis, published in a 2021 monograph", "Pushed back confirmed date of true copper smelting to 4900 BC, making Локалитет Беловоде код Петровца на Млави the earliest secure evidence of extractive metallurgy anywhere in the world", "Miners specifically favored black and green copper ores, reflecting deliberate cultural aesthetic preferences", "Rudnik Glava identified as one of the earliest known copper mines, mined at scale", "Tin bronze foil recovered at Pločnik dated to ~4650 BC, over 1,000 years before the Bronze Age, but the tradition was short-lived", "Copper mostly used for ornaments and status display, not replacing stone tools"]$cf$::jsonb
UNION ALL
SELECT 8359 AS id, count(*) AS matching_rows FROM news_items WHERE id = 8359 AND headline = $ch$China's 大汶口遗址公园 holds oldest elongated skulls claimed at 10,000 years old$ch$ AND summary = $cs$China's 大汶口遗址公园 holds oldest elongated skulls claimed at 10,000 years old. Host claims Dàrén Cùyū (Darren Cuyu) in China contains the oldest known elongated skulls, dated to approximately 10,000 years ago Host notes the site's top level was excavated first, meaning all archaeologists have passed through the oldest strata Host criticizes archaeological methodology of finding later-period artifacts in lower levels at this site$cs$ AND post_text = $cp$The oldest known elongated skulls in China date to approximately 12,000 years ago, not 10,000. The site name "Dàrén Cùyū (Darren Cuyu)" does not correspond to any verified archaeological site in available records, and the elongated skulls from this period are not associated with 大汶口遗址公园 culture, which dates to roughly 4,300–2,600 BCE. Claims about excavation methodology causing later artifacts to appear in lower strata remain unverified.$cp$ AND facts = $cf$["Host claims Dàrén Cùyū (Darren Cuyu) in China contains the oldest known elongated skulls, dated to approximately 10,000 years ago", "Host notes the site's top level was excavated first, meaning all archaeologists have passed through the oldest strata", "Host criticizes archaeological methodology of finding later-period artifacts in lower levels at this site", "Host argues this discovery pattern reflects excavation order, not chronological anomalies"]$cf$::jsonb
ORDER BY id;
